  "version": "0.6.1-beta.6",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.6.1-beta.5`\n\n### Features\n\n- keep an SSH tab's icon with its saved connection: the distribution its host runs and the icon picked under Edit Tab are saved in the profile, so its new tabs show them at once and every open tab of it changes together; the connection dialog can pick the icon too, and the saved distribution is dropped once the host or port changes ([fcdca81d](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/fcdca81da06302a1563144575b2c5dc43a6e4710))\n- show the logo of the Linux distribution an SSH host runs as its tab's icon: once the shell starts, tTerm reads /etc/os-release on a channel of its own, a server until then or for a host without one; the icon picker offers the distribution logos too, SSH tabs can get an icon of their own under Edit Tab, and turning tab icons off also stops the check ([f5eed87a](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/f5eed87a80efebfed1ae2f76b4d9666476128b66))\n\n### Fixes\n\n- show Linux Mint and other derivatives with their own logo: a host's ID and name now win over its ID_LIKE, where Linux Mint names Ubuntu and so showed Ubuntu's logo in the server monitor ([27f10318](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/27f1031861653558a093a3aae6c9058b2343b845))\n\n### Other changes\n\n- describe the AI coding agent integration in both READMEs: one-click hooks or plugins for Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode and pi, tab badges while an agent works or waits, notifications, use over SSH and tmux, and the badge settings; also link the License section to the new LICENSE file ([c20f9199](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/c20f919915630803b12e47e1ae48d9e6bc09fd70))\n- add the MIT LICENSE file the README already named, so GitHub detects the license, and declare it as \"license\": \"MIT\" in package.json, Cargo.toml and the Tauri bundle config, which writes it into the deb and rpm package metadata ([46e5393d](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/46e5393ddb79512e660f377480a19fcd8e92d090))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.6.1-beta.5...v0.6.1-beta.6](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.6.1-beta.5...v0.6.1-beta.6)",
